# .gitattributes — H_T workspace. Authority: Bootstrap Runbook §4.4.5.
# Force LF line endings. Rationale: hash-chain integrity per IS plan v2.2
# U-IS-08/09/10 requires deterministic byte-level state ledger writes;
# CRLF vs LF differences break SHA-256 chain verification.

*.py    text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# --- append-only ledger merge strategy (B-255) --------------------------------------
# These three ledgers are STRICTLY APPEND-ONLY: every writer opens them with O_APPEND /
# mode "a" and adds whole lines; nothing edits or removes an existing row (an
# adjudication is appended as its own `finding_adjudication` row, never an in-place
# rewrite). For that shape a merge is a UNION, never a choice — two lanes appending
# concurrently is the normal case, not a conflict, and resolving it by hand is both
# pure overhead and a chance to drop a row.
#
# Measured 2026-09-17: one held branch's appended rows fenced a sibling lane's
# selection gate on merge-gate-log.jsonl alone, and three such conflicts were resolved
# by hand in a single session.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED: .harness/arc-metrics.jsonl. It is whole-file rewritten
# (`arc_metrics.relabel_arc_type_close`, temp + os.replace), so union would keep BOTH
# the pre- and post-relabel row for one arc — and merge CLEAN while doing it, which is
# the SPLIT_BRAIN_LEDGER state that module exists to refuse. Adding a rewritten ledger
# here is silent corruption; tools/test_gitattributes_ledger_merge.py pins the split.
.harness/merge-gate-log.jsonl        merge=union
.harness/mutation-probe-log.jsonl    merge=union
.harness/codex_credential_gates.jsonl merge=union
